Platform: one-socket Xeon host with two QAT 420xx physical functions, each bound to
the 420xx driver with 4 SR-IOV VFs, vfio-pci loaded.

Sources (kernel paths are Linux v6.18 (torvalds/linux tag v6.18)):
- PF 0x4946 / VF 0x4947, driver name "420xx" (ADF_420XX_DEVICE_NAME):
  drivers/crypto/intel/qat/qat_common/adf_accel_devices.h; module qat_420xx:
  drivers/crypto/intel/qat/Kconfig. pci.ids names 4946 "420xx Series QAT" and 4947
  "420xx Series QAT Virtual Function".
- The plugin maps VF id 4947 to the 420xxvf kernel driver and accepts it as a QAT
  Gen4 VF: intel-device-plugins v0.37.1 cmd/qat_plugin/dpdkdrv/dpdkdrv.go.
- virtfn<n> links on the PF, sriov_numvfs: Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-pci.
- allocatable qat.intel.com/cy: the "sym;asym" cfg_services mapping in
  dpdkdrv.go, as in xeon-spr-accel.

Layout: sysfs paths and relative symlinks follow the driver core's naming, in
exactly the form tests/fixtures/capture.sh writes (the matrix test re-captures each
tree and requires an identical result).

Not from hardware: which Xeon carries 420xx (not settled in a primary source read
for this fixture, so there is no model name line and no ARK default), BDFs, the
core count, the kernel release string and the cpuinfo flags line (the xeon-gnr
subset).
